## ACCESSIBILITY REQUIREMENTS

### Every interactive element must have:

- A visible focus indicator (custom, not browser default — use `focus-visible`)
- Appropriate ARIA labels when the visual label is insufficient
- Minimum 44×44px touch target on mobile
- Keyboard operability (Tab, Shift+Tab, Enter, Space, Escape)
- Proper semantic HTML (`<button>` for actions, `<a>` for navigation — never swap)

### Color & contrast

- Text contrast ≥ 4.5:1 against background
- UI component contrast ≥ 3:1
- Never rely on color alone to convey meaning (pair with icon, text, or pattern)

### Motion

- Every Framer Motion component checks `prefers-reduced-motion`
- Provide a motion-disabled alternative that still communicates information
- Never auto-play video with sound
- Avoid parallax or large movement on scroll for users who opted out

### Forms

- Every input has an associated `<label>` (no placeholder-only labels)
- Error messages linked via `aria-describedby`
- Required fields marked programmatically (`aria-required` + visual indicator)
- Submission states announced to screen readers (`aria-live`)

### Testing

- Run `@axe-core/react` in development
- Manual keyboard-only navigation test before any PR
- Test with VoiceOver (macOS/iOS) and NVDA (Windows) on critical flows

